<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ziesar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ziesar is a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-an-der-havel">Brandenburg an der Havel</a>. From the 14th century it was the residence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Brandenburg, whose castle with its Gothic chapel survives and houses a museum of the medieval diocese.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ziesar.jpg" alt="Ziesar" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Andrschu assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stadtkirche_Heilig_Kreuz_Ziesar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
